---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
---

<div class="card-silver">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
    <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg bg-slate-200 flex items-center justify-center dark:bg-black/40">
      <Icon name="line-md:star-filled" class="text-slate-700 text-xl dark:text-white" />
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-0 dark:text-white">Managing Senior & Staff Engineers</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-800 dark:text-white">How I enabled high-performing engineers to do their best work</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-lg p-4 dark:bg-black/40">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2 dark:text-white">
          <Icon name="line-md:cog-loop" class="text-purple-600" />
          Autonomy with Alignment
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-gray-100">
          Set clear outcomes and constraints, then trusted them to own the "how." Weekly sync on blockers and cross-team dependencies, but avoided micromanagement.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-2 dark:text-gray-400">
          <em><strong>Example:</strong> Staff engineer owned RAG pipeline architecture, I removed obstacles and secured resources.</em>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-lg p-4 dark:bg-black/40">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2 dark:text-white">
          <Icon name="line-md:lightbulb-twotone" class="text-purple-600" />
          Strategic Context
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-white">
          Shared company/org strategy early and often so they could make informed tradeoffs. Invited them to roadmap planning, stakeholder meetings, and budget discussions.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-2 dark:text-gray-400">
          <em><strong>Example:</strong> When CFO flagged $50K/month LLM costs, I included Senior engineers in the cost review meeting—they proposed self-hosted solution because they understood the business constraint.</em>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-lg p-4 dark:bg-black/40">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2 dark:text-white">
          <Icon name="line-md:star-filled" class="text-purple-600" />
          Multiplier Opportunities
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-white">
          Created opportunities to lead: architecture reviews, mentoring junior engineers, technical RFC process ownership. Senior engineers led migration planning; Staff engineer established engineering standards.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-2 dark:text-gray-400">
          <em><strong>Example:</strong> Senior engineer ran weekly office hours and became the go-to expert, presented at engineering all-hands, and earned Staff promotion.</em>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white/80 rounded-lg p-4 dark:bg-black/40">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2 dark:text-white">
          <Icon name="line-md:heart-twotone" class="text-purple-600" />
          Recognition & Growth
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-white">
          Amplified their wins to leadership, ensured they got credit for their work. Pushed for comp adjustments and promotions backed by clear impact narratives. Connected them to career opportunities beyond my team.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mt-2 dark:text-gray-400">
          <em><strong>Example:</strong> Mid-level engineer led ci/cd integration. I highlighted their work in VP review, wrote promotion case showing $480K annual savings from their automation, secured promotion to Senior.</em>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
